  "problem": "The following table indicates the average number of hours per week each student, in a group of five, studies in a semester and the overall percentage each receives for their math classes. \n\n| **Study Time (h)** | **$3$** | **$5$** | **$7$** | **$8$** | **$10$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Overall Percentage** | $65$ | $60$ | $85$ | $80$ | $90$ |\n\nWhich of the following scatter plots represents this data?",
  "worked_solution": "We create a scatter diagram in the coordinate plane as follows:\n\n- First, we draw the independent variable (study time) along the horizontal axis.\n\n- Then, we draw the dependent variable (overall percentage) along the vertical axis.\n\n- Finally, we plot the points that correspond to the pairs from the data.\n\nThis gives us the following scatter plot.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/1b3771abe2f6ab985fd6dc4a0e196ec2311b05b89776b092786aac7c4028a3aa.png)",
